  "post": {
    "caption": "Scans found tigers under wool. In 2014, a metal detectorist found the Galloway Hoard in Scotland, a Viking age treasure of more than 100 objects buried around the year 900. One was a lidded silver pot wrapped in wool. Scans showed a fire altar with leopards and tigers under the wrapping, so the pot was likely made in Central Asia. Inside was a rock crystal jar about two inches tall, fitted with gold mesh and filigree, and scans found gold letters under its base that read, Bishop Hyguald had me made. Scotland bought the hoard in 2017 for 1.98 million pounds.",
